<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Android 12+ (API 31+). What leaves the phone in a backup or a transfer.

     The WebView's storage (app_webview/) holds two things in ONE database that
     cannot be split: the person's on-device budget and expenses, and — when
     signed in — the Supabase session, including its long-lived refresh token.

     Cloud backup stores a copy in the person's Google Drive, off the device, to
     be restored to any phone later. A refresh token there is a credential at
     rest somewhere we do not control, so app_webview/ is excluded. Signed-in
     data is unaffected (it syncs from the account); guest data is not carried
     by a cloud restore, which the privacy policy says.

     Device-to-device transfer is the person moving to a new phone, both devices
     in hand. Carrying everything there — guest data and the session — is the
     point of the feature and stays within their control, so it is allowed.

     Android 11 and below use backup_rules.xml, which cannot tell the two apart
     and therefore excludes the WebView storage from both. -->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" path="app_webview/" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <!-- No <device-transfer> element: Android then transfers everything,
         which is the intent. Listing includes instead would silently drop any
         storage domain the list forgot. -->
</data-extraction-rules>
